{
  "_help": [
    "What lives in the FISH tanks, and how many of each species FISH can take. Read by",
    "Scripts/Objects_And_Classes/Fishing/Fish_Shop_Tanks.gd (FishShopTanks).",
    "",
    "floors: map data name -> { stages, replace_at }.",
    "  stages: '<N>' -> { tank node name -> [ {species, pattern, max}, ... ] }.",
    "    N is the number of fish SENT TO FISH that stage needs. The stage in force is the",
    "    highest N the player has reached -- it REPLACES the lower lists outright, so a",
    "    stage lists every tank on that floor, including ones carried over from before.",
    "    A tank node is found by NAME anywhere in the floor's scene, so the tanks inside",
    "    Interior_0 can still be filled at stage 25.",
    "  replace_at: Interior_<N> numbers that REPLACE every lower interior on that floor",
    "    instead of being added on top (downstairs Interior_50 swaps out Interior_0).",
    "",
    "A species' CAP is the sum of its `max` over every row in the stages in force on both",
    "floors. Under the cap a catch is sent to FISH (+bonus); the catch that reaches it",
    "says 'Maximum X caught'; anything after says 'No room at FISH to send X'. A species",
    "with no row at all has a cap of 0.",
    "",
    "pattern: fish = swims (PokemonFishTank), may overlap other fish",
    "         wander = short slow steps in any direction, bumps into neighbours",
    "         idle_random = stands still, looks a random way now and then",
    "Each tank's movement area is its MOVEMENTZONE* ColorRect (hidden in game).",
    "",
    "The floors' Interior_<N> node names are the other half of this: renaming",
    "Interior_100 to Interior_150 moves that expansion (and its phone call) -- rename the",
    "stage key here and the fish_shop_<N>_* calls in Phone_Calls.json to match. With",
    "DebugMode on, entering a floor warns about anything that does not line up."
  ],
